[[:db/retract 17592186198632 :question/answer-fields 17592186194423] {:db/id 17592186401405 :question/problem "For the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}xy \\\\ {x}^{2}-y \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe total derivative ${f}^{′}$ is given by \n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}y & \\bbox[3pt,border: 1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}} \\\\ \\bbox[3pt,border: 1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}} & -1 \\\\ \\bbox[3pt,border: 1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}} & x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what are the missing entries?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198414 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-afc538b7-6818-5bf5-a45c-82af4af91e85"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-afc538b7-6818-5bf5-a45c-82af4af91e85" :question/id #uuid "afc538b7-6818-5bf5-a45c-82af4af91e85" :question/math-academy-id "q-163159" :question/problem "Consider the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}} \\\\ {e}^{{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}^{2}}\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the linear approximation of $f$ at  $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ ∗\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 1 \\\\ 1 & ∗\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]),\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({e}^{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}})=2{x}_{1}{e}^{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({e}^{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}})={e}^{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({e}^{{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}^{2}})={e}^{{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}^{2}},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({e}^{{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}^{2}})=-2{x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}{e}^{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}} & {e}^{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}} \\\\ {e}^{{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}^{2}} & -2{x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe linear approximation of $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n1+2+2=5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d6d03c68-c527-56d7-8eec-20b909744859"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d6d03c68-c527-56d7-8eec-20b909744859" :answer-field/id #uuid "d6d03c68-c527-56d7-8eec-20b909744859" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-18b3a6d3-2922-5952-9dd5-688afdd0e22e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3b47b2e0-7b7d-5338-9d25-ced74e84a6e9" "answer-f115dc76-a7c4-5fcd-bfa9-03dec29e7b4d" "answer-18b3a6d3-2922-5952-9dd5-688afdd0e22e" "answer-ec4d1f97-e95b-5ef1-8ea5-17d2a475dba0" "answer-5f1bfc1c-98a1-5b2b-8c25-93072e2631fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b47b2e0-7b7d-5338-9d25-ced74e84a6e9" :answer/id #uuid "3b47b2e0-7b7d-5338-9d25-ced74e84a6e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f115dc76-a7c4-5fcd-bfa9-03dec29e7b4d" :answer/id #uuid "f115dc76-a7c4-5fcd-bfa9-03dec29e7b4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18b3a6d3-2922-5952-9dd5-688afdd0e22e" :answer/id #uuid "18b3a6d3-2922-5952-9dd5-688afdd0e22e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec4d1f97-e95b-5ef1-8ea5-17d2a475dba0" :answer/id #uuid "ec4d1f97-e95b-5ef1-8ea5-17d2a475dba0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f1bfc1c-98a1-5b2b-8c25-93072e2631fd" :answer/id #uuid "5f1bfc1c-98a1-5b2b-8c25-93072e2631fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2}+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-fe2bd770-056c-540f-8c4f-31dd27239fe4" :activity/id #uuid "fe2bd770-056c-540f-8c4f-31dd27239fe4" :activity/title "The Derivative of a Multivariable Function" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049962 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-94cb74fe-b2ab-55cb-8a35-9664802